   "record": "e74eb7ac3fb7070fecd4a9562b4c2e568d97931443113bd3e9de2513cc8648ce",
   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; i1040gi p. 23, Community Property States, \"A registered domestic partner in Nevada, Washington, or California must generally report half the combined community income\"; p555 p. 2, Domicile, \"If you and your spouse (or your RDP) have different domiciles, check the laws of each\". The reply is right that the community rule turns on domicile; the gate is a refusal, not a computation, and it refuses every registered domestic partner of those states not filing jointly whether or not domiciled there (BUG-1089, decided by the coordinator under the owner's grant: refuse). A partner not domiciled there is refused though the rule may not apply: extra refusing, no amount computed wrongly.",
